From: zaken9090 <zaken9090@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] lavender-1026: AMP again (gold A73 = P cluster, silver A53 = E cluster), as topaz-0141 had it

XNU boots on the gold cluster now (1003) and can run all eight cores (ADT --all8). Without
__ARM_AMP__ the scheduler saw one homogeneous cluster and put the window server's render thread
on a 1.37 GHz A53 as often as on a 2.2 GHz A73: eight cores were slower than four in Settings.
With it, threads of the default and higher QoS go to P, background/utility and kernel threads
to E (recommended_pset_type() without CLPC), and P spills to E only when it is busy.
The ADT marks the cores 'P' / 'E' (mkadt_lavender.py --all8).

---
 pexpert/pexpert/arm64/SWEET.h | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/SWEET.h b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/SWEET.h
--- a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/SWEET.h
+++ b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/SWEET.h
@@ -43,8 +43,7 @@
  * silver A53 = E cluster (ADT cluster-type). The Edge scheduler then keeps
  * threads on P and spills to E only when P is busy (no CLPC recommends).
  */
-/* lavender: XNU boots on the silver A53 cluster only (gold runs at 1/4
- * clock, see lavender/dump probes); one homogeneous cluster, no AMP. */
+#define __ARM_AMP__               1
 #endif
 
 #define HAS_GIC_V3                1
